-- title:
--   Decomposition group generated by Frobenius at an unramified prime
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a number field which is Galois over $\mathbb{Q}$, let $\ell$ be a prime number, and let $Q$ be a prime ideal of the ring of integers $\mathcal{O}_L$ lying over the ideal $\ell\mathbb{Z} =$ `Ideal.span {(ℓ : ℤ)}` of $\mathbb{Z}$. Assume that the inertia subgroup `Q.inertia (L ≃ₐ[ℚ] L)` of $Q$ inside the group $L \simeq_{\text{alg}[\mathbb{Q}]} L$ of $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra automorphisms of $L$ is trivial. Since $Q$ lies over a nonzero prime of $\mathbb{Z}$ it is nonzero, so the residue ring $\mathcal{O}_L / Q$ is finite; this finiteness instance is supplied in the statement, and it is what makes the arithmetic Frobenius element `arithFrobAt ℤ (L ≃ₐ[ℚ] L) Q` available. The assertion is an equality of subgroups of $L \simeq_{\text{alg}[\mathbb{Q}]} L$: the stabiliser of $Q$ for the natural action on ideals of $\mathcal{O}_L$, that is the decomposition group of $Q$, coincides with the subgroup of integral powers (`Subgroup.zpowers`) of that arithmetic Frobenius element.
--
--   This is the classical statement that at an unramified prime the decomposition group is cyclic, generated by the Frobenius element. It underlies the counting of degree-one primes by fixed points of Frobenius, and is used in the Chebotarev-style density arguments of the Taylor–Wiles prime selection and in the production of a split place in the Langlands–Tunnell input.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_FrobeniusDensity_stabilizer_eq_zpowers_arithFrobAt.lean

import Definitions.Def_TaylorWiles_Primes
import Mathlib.NumberTheory.RamificationInertia.Galois
import Mathlib.GroupTheory.GroupAction.Basic

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

open NumberField Ideal
open scoped Pointwise
attribute [local instance 1001] NumberField.RingOfIntegers.instMulSemiringAction

theorem FrobeniusDensity.stabilizer_eq_zpowers_arithFrobAt
    {L : Type*} [Field L] [NumberField L] [IsGalois ℚ L]
    {ℓ : ℕ} (hℓ : ℓ.Prime) (Q : Ideal (𝓞 L)) [Q.IsPrime]
    [Q.LiesOver (FrobeniusDensity.ratPrimeIdeal ℓ)] (hinertia : Q.inertia (L ≃ₐ[ℚ] L) = ⊥) :
    haveI : Finite ((𝓞 L) ⧸ Q) :=
      FrobeniusDensity.finite_quotient_of_ne_bot
        (FrobeniusDensity.ne_bot_of_liesOver_ratPrimeIdeal hℓ)
    MulAction.stabilizer (L ≃ₐ[ℚ] L) Q
      = Subgroup.zpowers (arithFrobAt ℤ (L ≃ₐ[ℚ] L) Q) := by sorry
